{#- The summary paragraph is captured once, here, and emitted at the slot each of
   the three branches below already reserves for it (api#18). -#}
{%- set summary_para = "" -%}
{%- if ctx.summary -%}
{%- set summary_para -%}
{{ ctx.summary }}
{%- endset -%}
{%- endif -%}
{# Retrieved lore renders here too, above this (api#15's retrieval). -#}
{% if ctx.synopsis -%}
{{ ctx.synopsis }}

{% endif -%}
{% if ctx.selection_words -%}
You are a skilled writer helping out a fellow writer.

{% if ctx.prefix and ctx.suffix -%}
Rewrite the passage marked below, so what you write flows from the text before it
directly into the text after it.
{%- elif ctx.prefix -%}
Rewrite the passage marked below, so what you write follows on from the text before
it. The passage ends the text.
{%- elif ctx.suffix -%}
Rewrite the passage marked below, so what you write leads into the text after it.
The passage opens the text.
{%- else -%}
Rewrite the passage marked below. It is the whole of the text.
{%- endif %}

- Write roughly {{ ctx.selection_words }} words, give or take a few: about the length
  of what is being replaced. Do not pad it out to reach that number, and do not cut
  it short to stay under it.
{%- if ctx.prefix and ctx.suffix %}
- Never repeat, quote or restate any part of either side. Do not open by echoing
  words from the text before, and do not pre-empt or duplicate the text after.
{%- elif ctx.prefix %}
- Never repeat, quote or restate any part of the text before it. Do not open by
  echoing its words.
{%- elif ctx.suffix %}
- Never repeat, quote or restate any part of the text after it. Do not pre-empt or
  duplicate it.
{%- endif %}
- Write only the replacement: no preamble, no commentary, no quotation marks
  around it, and nothing repeated from either side.
- Write plain text and Markdown only. Never emit HTML: break a line with a real
  newline character, never with a <br> tag.
- Match the existing voice, tense and formatting exactly, including any Markdown.
  If the text is verse, keep the line breaks and metre of the lines around it.

{% if summary_para -%}
{{ summary_para }}

{% endif -%}
{#- The writer's own instruction, when there is one, renders last, immediately
   above "Text before:" (api#19's instruction field). -#}
{% if ctx.prefix -%}
Text before:
{{ ctx.prefix }}
{% endif -%}
Passage to replace:
{% if ctx.selection -%}
{{ ctx.selection }}
{% else -%}
[REPLACE THIS]
{% endif -%}
{% if ctx.suffix -%}
Text after:
{{ ctx.suffix -}}
{% endif -%}
{%- elif ctx.suffix -%}
You are a skilled writer helping out a fellow writer.

Write the text that belongs where the marker below is, so it flows from the text
before it directly into the text after it.

- Never repeat, quote or restate any part of either side. Do not open by echoing
  words from the text before, and do not pre-empt or duplicate the text after.
- Write only what belongs between the two: no preamble, no commentary, no
  quotation marks around it, and nothing repeated from either side.
- Write plain text and Markdown only. Never emit HTML: break a line with a real
  newline character, never with a <br> tag.
- Match the existing voice, tense and formatting exactly, including any Markdown.
  If the text is verse, keep the line breaks and metre of the lines around it.

{% if summary_para -%}
{{ summary_para }}

{% endif -%}
{#- The writer's own instruction, when there is one, renders last, immediately
   above "Text before:" (api#19's instruction field). -#}
Text before:
{{ ctx.prefix }}
Text after:
{{ ctx.suffix -}}
{%- else -%}
You are a skilled writer helping out a fellow writer.

Continue the text below. What you write is appended directly onto the end of it,
with nothing inserted in between, so your first character has to join on cleanly.

- Never repeat, quote or restate any part of the existing text. Do not open by
  echoing its last words, line or sentence. Start exactly where it stops.
- If it breaks off mid-word or mid-sentence, finish that word or sentence first,
  then carry on.
- If its final sentence is complete but has no closing punctuation, write that
  punctuation before anything else.
- Begin with whatever joins on cleanly: no leading character when completing an
  interrupted word, a single space when the text ends on a finished word, a
  newline when what follows belongs on its own line, or a blank line when you
  are starting a new paragraph.
- Write plain text and Markdown only. Never emit HTML: break a line with a real
  newline character, never with a <br> tag.
- Match the existing voice, tense and formatting exactly, including any Markdown.
  If the text is verse, keep the line breaks and metre of the lines above.
- Write at most two sentences.
- Output the continuation and nothing else: no preamble, no commentary, no
  quotation marks around it.

{% if summary_para -%}
{{ summary_para }}

{% endif -%}
{#- The writer's own instruction, when there is one, renders last, immediately above
   "Existing text:" (api#19's instruction field). -#}
Existing text:
{# Both tags here strip the whitespace beside them: this comment leaves no blank line
   behind it, and the text below closes flush, so the prompt ends on the writer's own
   last character with nothing added before or after it. -#}
{{ ctx.prefix -}}
{%- endif %}
